      "excludePrompt": "real artist or band names, existing song titles, flat chorus with no lift, monotonous melody, muddy low end, thin placeholder hook, famous artist imitation, dramatic power-ballad shouting",
      "lyrics": "[verse 1: Male Vocal]\nSteam rises slow above the cup I hold,\nLight moves across the table, soft and gold,\nI turn the spoon around without a sound,\nWaiting for the kitchen to wake.\n\n[pre-chorus: Female Vocal]\nSome mornings ask for nothing more,\nJust quiet time behind a closed door.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nMorning Holds Me Still before the day gets loud,\nThe kettle clicks, the light spills through the cloud,\nNothing here is rushing, nothing needs to prove,\nI let the morning tell me when to move.\n\n[verse 2: Female Vocal]\nThe paper waits, unread, beside the plate,\nI take my time, I never mind the wait,\nTwo cups still sit though only one gets used,\nSome habits stay, and I'm no longer confused.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nMorning Holds Me Still before the day gets loud,\nThe kettle clicks, the light spills through the cloud,\nNothing here is rushing, nothing needs to prove,\nI let the morning tell me when to move.\n\n[bridge: Male and Female Call and Response]\nMaybe today the phone will ring,\nMaybe today I'll hum a thing,\nUntil then I keep the kettle warm,\nMeeting the light before the storm.\n\n[final chorus: Male and Female Duet Harmony]\nMorning Holds Me Still before the day gets loud,\nThe kettle clicks, the light spills through the cloud,\nNothing here is rushing, nothing needs to prove,\nMorning Holds Me Still, and that is enough.",
