      "lyrics": "[intro]\n(instrumental)\n\n[verse 1]\nI found it folded behind a book,\nTucked away where I forgot to look,\nYour handwriting still slants like it did,\nI read it twice before I knew I hid.\n\n[pre-chorus]\nThe paper's soft, the ink turned gray,\nYet somehow none of it is gone.\n\n[chorus]\nThe window's open, letting in the light,\nSome Things Never Fade, no matter how they might,\nA voice I know still lives between these lines,\nSome things stay close no matter the time.\n\n[verse 2]\nI set my coffee down to hold it,\nCareful with the corners, soft and light,\nOutside a car goes by, still and slow,\nThe morning moves along against my will.\n\n[chorus]\nThe window's open, letting in the light,\nSome Things Never Fade, no matter how they might,\nA voice I know still lives between these lines,\nSome things stay close no matter how much time.\n\n[bridge]\nI used to think that letters lost their weight,\nBut this one proves that some things never wait,\nFolded soft, it waited just for me,\nNow I understand what it meant to be.\n\n[final chorus]\nSome Things Never Fade, the window's letting light,\nThe paper's soft, nothing feels slight,\nA voice I know still lives between these lines,\nSome Things Never Fade, not even given time.",
