      "excludePrompt": "real artist or band names, existing song titles, competing over-sung vocals, oversized ballad drums, flat chorus with no lift, muddy low end, thin placeholder hook, famous artist imitation",
      "lyrics": "[intro]\nI still remember the night the music started,\n\n[verse 1]\nYour collar crooked, your smile unsure,\nNeither of us had danced before,\nThe lights were low, the room was warm,\nTwo left feet caught up in the storm.\n\n[chorus]\nNobody told us how the steps should go,\nYou Found Your Feet before I found my nerve,\nAround and around, the whole room turned to gold,\nSomething about that night refused to grow old.\n\n[verse 2]\nYou laughed when I stepped on your shoe by chance,\nSaid it only made it a better dance,\nThe old tune played, unhurried and sweet,\nSomehow our steps agreed to meet.\n\n[chorus]\nNobody told us how the steps should go,\nYou Found Your Feet before I found my nerve,\nAround and around, the whole room turned to gold,\nSomething about that night refused to grow old.\n\n[breakdown]\nMaybe it's just one summer night,\nMaybe it's the start of something right,\nEither way you're holding on to me,\nEither way this is where we're meant to be.\n\n[final chorus]\nYou Found Your Feet before I found my nerve,\nNobody told us how the steps should go,\nAround and around, the whole room turned to gold,\nYou Found Your Feet, and I never let it go.",
