      "lyrics": "[intro: Male Vocal]\nThe whistle blows before I'm ready to go,\n\n[verse 1: Male Vocal]\nYou said you'd write as soon as you got there,\nYour hand still raised against the platform air,\nThe train pulls off before I'm ready to,\nI stand here longer than I meant to.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nThe whistle fades but I'm still standing still,\nHold This Moment Still until I lose the light,\nSomething about this parting takes its time,\nI'll hold this ache until it feels right.\n\n[verse 2: Female Vocal]\nYou pressed your hand against the window glass,\nI matched it there before the moment passed,\nThe whole platform empties, but I don't move,\nSome goodbyes take longer to prove.\n\n[bridge: Male and Female Call and Response]\nMaybe it's the distance, maybe it's the time,\nMaybe it's just hard to say goodbye,\nEither way I'm standing here alone,\nEither way this platform feels like home.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nThe whistle fades but I'm still standing still,\nHold This Moment Still until I lose the light,\nSomething about this parting takes its time,\nI'll hold this ache until it feels right.\n\n[final chorus: Male and Female Duet Harmony]\nHold This Moment Still while the whistle fades,\nStanding here until I lose the light,\nSomething about this parting takes its time,\nHold This Moment Still, a little while.",
