      "excludePrompt": "real artist or band names, existing song titles, competing over-sung vocals, oversized ballad drums, flat chorus with no lift, muddy low end, thin placeholder hook, famous artist imitation",
      "lyrics": "[intro]\nShe seals the letter with a shaking hand,\n\n[verse 1]\nShe walks it past the fence, the old oak gap,\nThe corner mailbox waits there, cold and blue,\nShe stands a moment, thinking it through,\nWondering if her nerve will hold.\nThe street stays quiet, the morning holds its breath.\n\n[chorus]\nWhatever happens, whatever the reply,\nOne Small Risk before she lets it die,\nThe nerve won't last, so she takes the chance,\nTrusting the words to make their own advance.\n\n[verse 2]\nThree days of waiting by the window pane,\nWatching for the mailman through the rain,\nThen comes an answer folded soft and small,\nProof that reaching out was worth it all.\nShe reads it twice just to make it true.\n\n[chorus]\nWhatever happens, whatever the reply,\nOne Small Risk before she lets it die,\nThe nerve won't last, so she takes the chance,\nTrusting the words to make their own advance.\n\n[final chorus]\nOne Small Risk, and now the answer's here,\nWhatever happens, there is nothing left to fear,\nThe porch light glows a little warmer now,\nThe nerve was worth it, she takes the chance,\nOne Small Risk became a second chance.",
