      "excludePrompt": "real artist or band names, existing song titles, electric rock distortion, stadium drums, flat chorus with no lift, muddy low end, thin placeholder hook, famous artist imitation",
      "lyrics": "[intro]\n(instrumental)\n\n[verse 1: Female Vocal]\nI watch the road from the porch chair every day,\nWaiting on the truck to come my way,\nYou said you'd write as soon as you got there,\nSo I keep watching, rocking in this chair.\nThe mailbox shadow stretches long and thin.\n\n[pre-chorus: Male Vocal]\nNo letter yet but I don't mind the wait,\nTomorrow always feels like it's not too late.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nThe dust kicks up when the truck turns the bend,\nWatching For You, a promise I intend,\nEvery afternoon I keep the porch light on,\nHoping that today's the day it's gone.\n\n[verse 2: Male Vocal]\nThe neighbors wave but I barely notice them,\nMy heart still jumps like it did back then,\nSome days there's nothing, some days there's a line,\nEither way I keep on watching for a sign.\n\n[chorus: Male and Female Duet]\nThe dust kicks up when the truck turns the bend,\nWatching For You, a promise I intend,\nEvery afternoon I keep the porch light on,\nHoping that today's the day it's gone.\n\n[key-lift final chorus: Male and Female Duet Harmony]\nWatching For You, the dust kicks up again,\nThe truck turns the bend, a promise I intend,\nEvery afternoon I keep the porch light on,\nWatching For You, watching for you.",
